<!--
    kuna relocatable-object loader, GH-904: the calls and addresses of a
    PowerPC or MIPS object file (.o) are relocations the loader did not
    apply.  Every `bl`/`jal` kept the placeholder the compiler wrote (a branch
    to itself, or to 0), so calls printed as sub_<self> or sub_0, globals as
    dat_0, a PIC MIPS call through the GOT as (*(void *)0x3c020000)(), and a
    PowerPC64 ELFv1 object, whose function symbols name .opd descriptors,
    decompiled no function at all.  The caller evidence of option bejoin
    callers saw no call site, so add64's big-endian pair stayed joined
    low word first.

    The loader now applies the PowerPC REL24/PLTREL24/LOCAL24PC, REL14,
    ADDR16 and REL16 halves and data words, the MIPS 26, PC16, HI16/LO16
    pairs (REL addends), GPREL, and the GOT forms (CALL16, GOT16, GOT_DISP,
    GOT_PAGE/OFST) against a synthetic _gp and GOT, and maps each ELFv1
    descriptor symbol to its code.

    Stage: P1 program prep (relocatable-object loader); a strict loader fix,
    no option.  Single pass.

    Images: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/relocobj_*.o, from
    relocobj_calls.c (see relocobj.provenance).

    Assert #1: PPC32 -fno-pic: store calls add64 and stores sink64 high word
      first; add64 returns its sum high word first (its caller reads r4).
    Assert #2: PPC32 -fPIC (PLTREL24): callint calls extint.
    Assert #3: MIPS32 BE gcc -fno-pic (R_MIPS_26, HI16/LO16): store calls
      add64 and reads its pair $2 high; callint calls extint.
    Assert #4: MIPSel clang PIC (CALL16 through the GOT): wrap calls ext64.
    Assert #5: PowerPC64 ELFv1: store, found at add64's code, calls add64.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">4e80002000000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
